>> title: Madras Curry Powder
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: indian, curry, spice blend, toasted, pantry
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: madras, madrass, curry powder
>> pairs-with: japanese-beef-curry
>> servings: 24
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: narrow — three minutes on the whole spices and one on the ground, and the dried chiles in this are the limit rather than the seeds; a batch taken dark is bitter in every curry it is spooned into for as long as the jar lasts
>> step.1: toast in a dry skillet 3 min
>> step.2: add, toast 1 min more
>> step.3: cool, grind fine
>> step.4: whisk in

Toast @coriander seeds{1/4%cup}(24 g), @cumin seeds{2%Tbs}(12 g), @black mustard seeds{1%tsp}, @fenugreek seeds{1%tsp}, and @black peppercorns{1%tsp} in a dry #skillet{} over medium heat until the mustard seeds pop, about ~{3%min}.

Add @dried red chiles{8}(stemmed; Kashmiri or byadgi) and @dried curry leaves{15} to @&(~1)toasted spices{} and toast ~{1%min}, until the chiles darken a shade.

Cool @&(~1)spices{} completely, then grind to a fine powder in a #spice grinder{}.

Whisk @ground turmeric{1%Tbs} and @ground ginger{1%tsp} into @&(~1)powder{}.
